idates if the input n is a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Input must be an integer, but got type {type(n).__name__}.\")\n        if n < 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Input must be a non-negative integer, but got {n}.\")\n        return n\nclass CacheRepository:\n    \"\"\"Abstract base class for caching Catalan numbers.\"\"\"\n    def get(self, n: int) -> int | None:\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def set(self, n: int, value: int) -> None:\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def clear(self) -> None:\n        raise NotImplementedError\nclass InMemoryCacheRepository(CacheRepository):\n    \"\"\"In-memory implementation of CacheRepository.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._store: dict[int, int] = {}\n\n    def get(self, n: int) -> int | None:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a cached Catalan number by its index n.\"\"\"\n        return self._store.get(n)\n\n    def set(self, n: int, value: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stores a Catalan number in the cache.\"\"\"\n        self._store[n] = value\n\n    def clear(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Clears all entries from the cache.\"\"\"\n        self._store.clear()\nclass CatalanService:\n    \"\"\"Service layer for computing Catalan numbers, handling caching and strategy selection.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, cache_repo: CacheRepository, strategy: str):\n        self._cache = cache_repo\n        self._strategy = strategy\n\n    def get_catalan(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves the nth Catalan number, using cache or computing it.\"\"\"\n        cached_value = self._cache.get(n)\n        if cached_value is not None:\n            return cached_value\n\n        if self._strategy == \"dp\":\n            result = self._compute_via_dp(n)\n        elif self._strategy == \"binomial\":\n            result = self._compute_via_binomial(n)\n        else:\n            result = self._compute_via_dp(n)\n\n        self._cache.set(n, result)\n        return result\n\n    def _compute_via_dp(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the nth Catalan number using dynamic programming.\"\"\"\n        return MathUtils.dp_catalan(n)\n\n    def _compute_via_binomial(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the nth Catalan number using the binomial coefficient formula.\"\"\"\n        return MathUtils.binomial(2 * n, n) // (n + 1)\nclass CatalanController:\n    \"\"\"Public API entrypoint for computing Catalan numbers.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, cache_repo: CacheRepository = None, strategy: str = None):\n        self.cache_repo = cache_repo or InMemoryCacheRepository()\n        self.strategy = strategy or STRATEGY_DEFAULT\n        self.service = CatalanService(self.cache_repo, self.strategy)\n\n    def get_catalan(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Validates input and returns the nth Catalan number.\"\"\"\n        validated_n = ValidatorUtils.validate_non_negative_int(n)\n        return self.service.get_catalan(validated_n)\n_default_controller = CatalanController()\ndef catalan_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Returns the nth Catalan number.\"\"\"\n    return _default_controller.get_catalan(n)", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "Mbpp/586": [{"task_id": "Mbpp/586", "solution": "from typing import List, Any\ndef split_Arr(arr: List[Any], n: int) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"Splits a list at the nth element and adds the first part to the end.\n\n    This performs a left rotation of the list by 'n' positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    length = len(arr)\n    if length == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate the effective split point using modulo to handle\n    # positive or negative 'n', and 'n' larger than list length.\n    k = n % length\n\n    # Split the list into two parts and concatenate them in the desired order.\n    return arr[k:] + arr[:k]", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "Mbpp/585": [{"task_id": "Mbpp/585", "solution": "class ItemModel:\n    \"\"\"Represents a validated item with a name, price, and optional extra fields.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, name: str, price: float, extras: dict = None) -> None:\n        self._name = name\n        self._price = float(price)\n        self._extras = extras or {}\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Converts the ItemModel instance back to a dictionary, preserving extras.\"\"\"\n        return {\"name\": self._name, \"price\": self._price, **self._extras}\nclass ItemFactory:\n    \"\"\"Provides a static method to create ItemModel instances from raw dictionaries.\"\"\"\n    @staticmethod\n    def from_dict(raw: dict) -> ItemModel:\n        name = raw.get(\"name\")\n        price = raw.get(\"price\")\n        extras = {k: v for k, v in raw.items() if k not in (\"name\", \"price\")}\n        return ItemModel(name, price, extras)\ndef expensive_items(items: list[dict], n: int) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the n most expensive items in a given dataset.\n    The function sorts items by price in descending order and returns the top n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not items or n <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Convert raw dictionaries to ItemModel instances for consistent processing.\n    models = [ItemFactory.from_dict(item) for item in items]\n\n    # Sort the ItemModel instances by their price in descending order.\n    # Python's sorted() is a stable sort, preserving original order for equal prices.\n    sorted_models = sorted(models, key=lambda m: m._price, reverse=True)\n\n    # Take the top 'n' items from the sorted list.\n    top_n_models = sorted_models[:n]\n\n    # Convert the resulting ItemModel instances back into dictionaries.\n    return [model.to_dict() for model in top_n_models]", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "Mbpp/587": [{"task_id": "Mbpp/587", "solution": "def list_tuple(input_list: list) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Convert a Python list to a tuple.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If input_list is not a list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"input_list must be a list\")\n    return tuple(input_list)", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "Mbpp/436": [{"task_id": "Mbpp/436", "solution": "def neg_nos(numbers, forgiving: bool = False):\n    import json\n    import uuid\n    from datetime import datetime\n    from typing import Any, List, Dict, Optional, Tuple\n    from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n\n    class InputValidationError(Exception):\n        \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, message: str):\n            super().__init__(message)\n            self.message = message\n\n    @dataclass\n    class NumberListDTO:\n        \"\"\"DTO for a list of numbers with metadata.\"\"\"\n        id: str\n        numbers: List[float]\n        created_at: datetime = field(default_factory=datetime.utcnow)\n\n        def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n            \"\"\"Serializes the DTO to a dictionary.\"\"\"\n            return {\"id\": self.id, \"numbers\": self.numbers, \"created_at\": self.created_at.isoformat()}\n\n    class Utils:\n        \"\"\"Utility class for number validation and coercion.\"\"\"\n        SUPPORTED_NUMERIC_TYPES = (int, float)\n\n        @staticmethod\n        def coerce_to_number(value: Any, forgiving: bool=False) -> float:\n            \"\"\"Converts a value to float, optionally allowing string coercion.\"\"\"\n            if isinstance(value, Utils.SUPPORTED_NUMERIC_TYPES):\n                return float(value)\n            if forgiving and isinstance(value, str):\n                s = value.strip()\n                try:\n                    return float(s)\n                except ValueError:\n                    raise InputValidationError(f\"Cannot coerce '{value}' to number\")\n            raise InputValidationError(f\"Unsupported value type: {type(value)}\")\n\n        @staticmethod\n        def validate_numbers(numbers: Any, forgiving: bool=False) -> List[float]:\n            \"\"\"Validates and coerces an input to a list of floats.\"\"\"\n            if isinstance(numbers, str):\n                try:\n                    parsed = json.loads(numbers)\n                except Exception:\n                    parts = [p.strip() for p in numbers.split(\",\") if p.strip() != \"\"]\n                    return [Utils.coerce_to_number(p, forgiving) for p in parts]\n                numbers = parsed\n            if not hasattr(numbers, \"__iter__\") or isinstance(numbers, (bytes, bytearray)):\n                raise InputValidationError(\"Input is not iterable\")\n            result = []\n            for v in numbers:\n                result.append(Utils.coerce_to_number(v, forgiving))\n            return result\n\n        @staticmethod\n        def is_negative(n: float) -> bool:\n            \"\"\"Checks if a number is negative.\"\"\"\n            return n < 0.0\n\n    class InMemoryResultRepository:\n        \"\"\"In-memory repository for storing recent results.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, max_items: int = 100):\n            self._store: Dict[str, List[float]] = {}\n            self._max_items = max_items\n\n        def save_result(self, input_id: str, result: List[float]) -> None:\n            \"\"\"Saves a result to the repository, managing max_items.\"\"\"\n            if len(self._store) >= self._max_items:\n                oldest = next(iter(self._store))\n                self._store.pop(oldest, None)\n            self._store[input_id] = result\n\n        def get_result(self, input_id: str) -> Optional[List[float]]:\n            \"\"\"Retrieves a result by its ID.\"\"\"\n            return self._store.get(input_id)\n\n        def list_recent(self, limit: int = 10) -> List[Tuple[str, List[float]]]:\n            \"\"\"Lists the most recent results.\"\"\"\n            items = list(self._store.items())\n            return items[-limit:]\n\n    class NegativeNumberService:\n        \"\"\"Service for extracting negative numbers from a list.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, repo: InMemoryResultRepository):\n            self._repo = repo\n\n        def extract_negatives(self, numbers: List[Any], forgiving: bool=False) -> List[float]:\n            \"\"\"Extracts negative numbers, validates input, and saves results.\"\"\"\n            validated = Utils.validate_numbers(numbers, forgiving)\n            negatives = [n for n in validated if Utils.is_negative(n)]\n            dto = NumberListDTO(id=f\"nl-{uuid.uuid4().hex}\", numbers=negatives)\n            self._repo.save_result(dto.id, dto.numbers)\n            return negatives\n\n    class NegativeNumberController:\n        \"\"\"Controller for handling negative number extraction requests.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, service: NegativeNumberService):\n            self._service = service\n\n        def get_negatives(self, numbers_input: Any, forgiving: bool=False) -> List[float]:\n            \"\"\"Processes input to extract negative numbers.\"\"\"\n            return self._service.extract_negatives(numbers_input, forgiving)\n\n    # Instantiate dependencies locally within the function scope\n    _repo = InMemoryResultRepository()\n    _service = NegativeNumberService(repo=_repo)\n    _controller = NegativeNumberController(service=_service)\n\n    return _controller.get_negatives(numbers_input=numbers, forgiving=forgiving)", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "Mbpp/588": [{"task_id": "Mbpp/588", "solution": "from typing import List, Union, Any, Iterable\nNumber = Union[int, float]\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input conditions as per design.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\nclass Validator:\n    \"\"\"Validates and coerces input values into a list of numbers.\"\"\"\n    def validate_numbers(self, values: Iterable[Any]) -> List[Number]:\n        if values is None:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input is None\")\n        nums = []\n        for v in values:\n            num = self._coerce_number(v)\n            nums.append(num)\n        if not nums:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input list is empty\")\n        return nums\n\n    def _coerce_number(self, value: Any) -> Number:\n        if isinstance(value, (int, float)):\n            return value\n        if isinstance(value, str):\n            s = value.strip()\n            try:\n                if '.' in s:\n                    return float(s)\n                return int(s)\n            except ValueError:\n                try:\n                    return float(s)\n                except ValueError:\n                    raise InvalidInputError(f\"Value '{value}' is not numeric\")\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"Unsupported value type: {type(value).__name__}\")\nclass ListStats:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates a numeric list and provides statistics like min, max, and range.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, numbers: List[Number]) -> None:\n        self._numbers = list(numbers)\n\n    def count(self) -> int:\n        return len(self._numbers)\n\n    def min(self) -> Number:\n        if not self._numbers:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"No elements to determine min\")\n        return min(self._numbers)\n\n    def max(self) -> Number:\n        if not self._numbers:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"No elements to determine max\")\n        return max(self._numbers)\n\n    def range(self) -> Number:\n        return self.max() - self.min()\nclass BigDiffService:\n    \"\"\"Performs the core business logic of computing the difference.\"\"\"\n    def compute_difference(self, numbers: List[Number]) -> Number:\n        if not numbers:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"List must not be empty for difference computation.\")\n        stats = ListStats(numbers)\n        return stats.range()\nclass BigDiffController:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates input validation and delegates to the service for computation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, validator: Validator = None, service: BigDiffService = None) -> None:\n        self._validator = validator or Validator()\n        self._service = service or BigDiffService()\n\n    def compute_range(self, values: Iterable[Any]) -> Number:\n        numbers: List[Number] = self._validator.validate_numbers(values)\n        return self._service.compute_difference(numbers)\ndef big_diff(values: List[Number]) -> Number:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the difference between the largest and smallest value in a given list.\n    This function acts as the public API facade, delegating to internal components.\n    \"\"\"\n    controller = BigDiffController()\n    return controller.compute_range(values)", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "Mbpp/589": [{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "import math\ndef perfect_squares(low: int, high: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds perfect squares within a given range [low, high] inclusive.\n    Only non-negative perfect squares are considered.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(low, int) or not isinstance(high, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"low and high must be integers\")\n    if low > high:\n        raise ValueError(\"low must be <= high\")\n\n    if high < 0:\n        return []\n\n    effective_low = max(0, low)\n\n    start_k = math.isqrt(effective_low)\n    if start_k * start_k < effective_low:\n        start_k += 1\n\n    end_k = math.isqrt(high)\n\n    if end_k < start_k:\n        return []\n\n    squares = [k * k for k in range(start_k, end_k + 1)]\n\n    return squares", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "fail", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": [[1, 0]]}], "Mbpp/591": [{"task_id": "Mbpp/591", "soluti